  "assessment": [
    "2048 bytes is now a credible operational candidate for both built-in workers, including ordinary non-floating Roo connection logging and warnings.",
    "The inspected receive stderr path leaves about 256 bytes, so callbacks, wall-clock implementations, log sinks, floats, SDK verbosity and different compiler/SDK configurations require their own budget.",
    "Preserving the examined fatal core dump needs more task stack or a dedicated SDK core-dump stack. A short connect() disconnect callback can instead notify application code to handle peer reset outside the UART task.",
    "The library and benchmark retain 4096-byte reservations; no 2048-byte hardware validation is implied. Changing both reservations to 2048 saves 4096 nominal stack bytes per endpoint, with allocator effects requiring measurement."
  ]
